pulse-active (1.1.3) unstable; urgency=low

  * Fix: the dashboard no longer freezes when the terminal window is resized.
    The resize handler now only flags the change; the screen size is read and
    the dashboard is redrawn right after, at the new size.

 -- Carlos Corral <corral1976@gmail.com>  Sat, 21 Nov 2026 14:00:00 -0600

pulse-active (1.1.2) unstable; urgency=low

  * TTY mode: the system information is now laid out to the right of the
    heart, aligned in fixed columns, and the whole screen is pure ASCII.
  * TTY mode: progress bars are aligned and no longer repeat the percentage.
  * The dashboard adapts to the terminal height and to window resizing, so
    the screen no longer scrolls on small terminals.
  * Lower CPU use: the main loop reads CPU, memory, network, uptime and
    frequency without spawning external processes.
  * Colour codes are emitted once per bar segment instead of once per cell.
  * New --no-intro option to skip the start-up animation.
  * The start-up animation reuses the dashboard code.
  * Key presses are no longer echoed while the dashboard is running.
  * Colour support falls back to COLORTERM/TERM when tput is not available.
  * Clean exit when the terminal hangs up (SIGHUP).
  * An invalid or missing --interval value now exits with status 2, as the
    manual page documents.
  * BUILD_DEB.sh refuses to build when the changelog and src/pulse versions
    differ.
  * install_pulse.sh: the temporary build directory is readable by apt.
  * Fix: wrong weekday in the 1.0.0 changelog entry.
  * Code cleanup across all scripts.

 -- Carlos Corral <corral1976@gmail.com>  Sat, 21 Nov 2026 12:00:00 -0600

pulse-active (1.1.1) unstable; urgency=low

  * Fix: the dashboard no longer flickers. Frames are built once per tick and
    written in a single synchronized update, without clearing the screen
    first; the heartbeat only swaps the precomputed frames.
  * TTY mode redraws in place instead of clearing the screen on every refresh.

 -- Carlos Corral <corral1976@gmail.com>  Fri, 20 Nov 2026 15:30:00 -0600

pulse-active (1.1.0) unstable; urgency=low

  * Portability: new Makefile (PREFIX/DESTDIR) and generic installer that
    work on any Linux distribution; the .deb is now just one install method.
  * Source moved to src/pulse; the .deb is staged in a temporary directory.
  * New --once option and automatic quiet mode when stdout is not a terminal.
  * Fix: quiet mode no longer enters the alternate screen or prints escape
    codes into pipes.
  * Fix: busy loop (100% CPU) when stdin was not a terminal.
  * Fix: sensor/disk/battery caches never persisted (they ran in subshells).
  * Fix: GPU temperature no longer falls back to the NVMe sensor; CPU/GPU
    temperatures are read from hwmon without needing lm-sensors.
  * Fix: no more invented resolution/desktop values; real values from
    xrandr, xdpyinfo or DRM, otherwise N/A.
  * Fix: network rate is per second and ignores the loopback interface.
  * Fix: script no longer aborts without $USER, $SHELL or hostname(1).
  * Quiet output: NET now reports KB/s and the temperature field is TEMP:.

 -- Carlos Corral <corral1976@gmail.com>  Sat, 24 Oct 2026 12:00:00 -0600

